  "flow_summary": "The interviewer successfully navigated a challenging, confused patient persona by consistently rephrasing questions and maintaining patience. However, the system failed to handle the standardized questionnaires (PHQ-9 and GAD-7) efficiently, repeatedly re-asking questions and failing to maintain the context of the scale, which led to a tedious and repetitive experience.",
  "issues": [
    {
      "severity": "moderate",
      "category": "questionnaire_management",
      "evidence": "The system repeatedly re-asked PHQ-9 and GAD-7 items when the patient expressed confusion, rather than simplifying the delivery or maintaining the scale context effectively. For example: 'PHQ-9 Question 1: Over the last two weeks, how often have you been bothered by little interest or pleasure in doing things? ... Please choose 0, 1, 2, or 3.'"
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "category": "redundancy",
      "evidence": "In the PHQ-9 and GAD-7 sections, the system frequently re-stated the full question text multiple times in a single turn or across consecutive turns, which was unnecessary and contributed to the patient's confusion."
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "category": "flow",
      "evidence": "The transition after the patient's disclosure of suicidal intent was slightly jarring: 'Thank you for telling me. Your immediate safety is important... Thank you for explaining that. I’ve recorded what you shared. What do you hope to get out of your appointment?'"
    }
